OL,3,GFEATURES CThe introduction of colour on
OL,4,CBBC One and ITV
OL,5,
OL,6,GFOOTNOTES
OL,8,FThe vast majority of BBC One evening
OL,9,Fprogrammes were broadcast in colour
OL,10,Ffrom 15th November 1969.
OL,12,FThere were a few exceptions ` Z Cars
OL,13,Fremained in black and white for a few
OL,14,Fmore weeks although other drama was in
OL,15,Fcolour.
OL,17,FWithin a few months, it was very
OL,18,Funusual for a new network programme `
OL,19,Fother than a schools or adult education
OL,20,Fprogramme ` to be in black and white.
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,122,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12116
SC,0016
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F121A1768742397
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G16/18
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe introduction of colour on
OL,4,CBBC One and ITV
OL,5,
OL,6,FThere were conspicuous exceptions.
OL,8,FBlue Peter did not go into colour until
OL,9,FSeptember 1970.
OL,11,FThere is some ambiguity concerning when
OL,12,Fthe studio presentation of the network
OL,13,Fportion of Nationwide went into colour.
OL,14,FThe programme was not billed as a
OL,15,Fcolour programme and a lot of the
OL,16,Freports and interviews from the regions
OL,17,Fwere in black and white for many years.
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,122,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12117
SC,0017
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F121A1768742397
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G17/18
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe introduction of colour on
OL,4,CBBC One and ITV
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhile no colour recordings of
OL,7,FNationwide in this era are believed to
OL,8,Fexist, the BBC archive holds some film
OL,9,Freports from Nationwide in 1969/70
OL,10,Fwhich were in colour.
OL,12,FGenerally when BBC One colour
OL,13,Ftransmissions spread to a new region,
OL,14,Fthe regional output initially stayed in
OL,15,Fmonochrome.
OL,17,FAnother Interesting point...
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,122,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12118
SC,0018
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F121A1768742397
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                G18/18
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe introduction of colour on
OL,4,CBBC One and ITV
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhile there were restrictions on full
OL,7,Fcolour transmissions before 15th
OL,8,FNovember 1969, these did not apply to
OL,9,Fthe spread of colour afterwards.
OL,11,FPresumably each main transmitter opened
OL,12,Fafterwards would be putting out BBC One
OL,13,FUHF in full for a week or two before
OL,14,Fentering official programme service `
OL,15,Fobviously with the caveat that the
OL,16,Fservice was liable to interruption.
OL,18,FHowever I believe it was different on
OL,19,FITV initially ` more clearly
OL,20,Fengineering tests up to the official
OL,21,Flocal launch. Ad breaks were apparently
OL,22,Fcovered with the test card or bars.
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
